<%- include('partials/head') %>

<section class="hiw-hero">
  <p class="hiw-step-label">How it works</p>
  <h1>A game you play in real life.<br>Five steps from payslip to notice period.</h1>
  <p class="lead">NoBossly turns getting out of the 9 to 5 into ten levels you climb with real accomplishments &mdash; your first quest, your first sprint, your first non-salary dollar. Built to be played in evenings and weekends, while the job is still paying the rent. The community keeps you honest. You play.</p>
  <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:1.5rem">
    <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/paths">Find your path &mdash; it's free &rarr;</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/community">See the community</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single" style="margin-top:2rem">
  <div>
    <p class="hiw-step-label">Step 1</p>
    <h2>&#x1F9ED; Pick your path</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:.6rem"><strong>One choice to start.</strong> Which of nine paths you are on &mdash; creator, freelancer, coach, local service, shop, online store, software, product, or still deciding. Everything below is matched to it: your quest board, your ladder, and the other members climbing alongside you.</p>
    <p class="muted">No quiz, no waiting on a report. Pick a path and you're straight into the product &mdash; no report to wait on, no forms to fill out first.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row">
  <div>
    <p class="hiw-step-label">Step 2</p>
    <h2>&#x2694;&#xFE0F; Take on your first quest</h2>
    <p class="muted">Your quest board fills in immediately &mdash; core quests everyone on your path takes, plus electives matched to your business as you set it up. <strong>You</strong> pick the idea, always. Nobody drafts it for you and nobody grades it; the fit test is the peer-review queue and the Wins wall, where real members tell you honestly whether it holds up.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li>Core quests, filtered to your level as you climb</li>
      <li>Electives matched to your path and business</li>
      <li>Cohort quests &mdash; join a group starting the same day</li>
      <li>Real feedback from other members, not a model guessing at your situation</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="card" style="align-self:center;padding:1.5rem">
    <span class="tag">Sample quest board</span>
    <h3 style="margin:.6rem 0 .25rem">Level 2 &mdash; Validated</h3>
    <ul class="task-list" style="margin:.6rem 0 0">
      <li class="task done"><button class="task-check">&#x2713;</button><div><strong>Validate your idea</strong></div></li>
      <li class="task"><button class="task-check"></button><div><strong>Get 3 Feedback Sessions</strong> <span class="tag">peer review</span></div></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted small" style="margin:.7rem 0 0">&#x1F4AC; Two peers have already weighed in on your landing page.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single">
  <div>
    <p class="hiw-step-label">Step 3</p>
    <h2>&#x1F3C3; Run your first sprint</h2>
    <p class="muted">A sprint is a 7-day push toward one thing you decide, with your own tasks on it. Name it, add what needs doing, and check things off as you go &mdash; sized to the hours you actually have, not a template written for someone who already quit.</p>
    <div class="grid" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <div class="card">
        <h4>You name the goal</h4>
        <p class="muted small">What does done look like by the end of the week? You decide, not a generated plan.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>You add the tasks</h4>
        <p class="muted small">Whatever moves the goal forward &mdash; a landing page, five outreach messages, a pricing page.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>Velocity tracks itself</h4>
        <p class="muted small">See what percentage of the week's tasks actually got done, sprint over sprint.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>Daily check-ins</h4>
        <p class="muted small">+15 XP and a streak that survives one busy Tuesday &mdash; one freeze a month.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row">
  <div>
    <p class="hiw-step-label">Step 4</p>
    <h2>&#x1F4AC; Get real feedback, from real people</h2>
    <p class="muted">Generic advice is easy to ignore. A stranger on the same ladder telling you your pricing page doesn't say what you sell isn't. The peer-review queue pairs you with other members: post what you're working on, get honest answers, and give reviews of your own &mdash; it earns XP and clears a quest.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li><strong>Ask for feedback</strong> &mdash; on your idea, your pitch, your landing page, your pricing</li>
      <li><strong>Give a review</strong> &mdash; earns XP and counts toward your own ladder</li>
      <li><strong>Testimonials</strong> &mdash; collect proof from people you've helped or sold to</li>
      <li><strong>A weekly reading list</strong> from 100+ guides in the library. Free.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="card" style="padding:1.5rem;align-self:center">
    <h4 style="margin:0 0 .4rem">&#x1F4AC; Sample review</h4>
    <p class="muted small" style="margin:0 0 1rem">On: “Landing page for my bookkeeping side gig”</p>
    <p class="muted small" style="margin:0">“The headline buries what you actually do &mdash; I had to scroll to figure out you're a bookkeeper, not an accountant. Lead with the outcome, not the credential.”</p>
    <p class="muted small" style="margin:.7rem 0 0">&mdash; a fellow member, 3 rungs ahead of you</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single">
  <div>
    <p class="hiw-step-label">Step 5</p>
    <h2>&#x1F3AE; Climb your own ladder</h2>
    <p class="muted">Ten rungs between a job you want out of and a notice period &mdash; and they are named for what you are actually building. A plumber&rsquo;s fifth rung is not a podcaster&rsquo;s. What never changes: <strong>XP alone can never buy a rung.</strong> Every one gates on something that happened in the real world.</p>
    <div class="grid" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <div class="card">
        <h4>&#x1F3AC; The creator climbs&hellip;</h4>
        <p class="muted small">Lurker &rarr; Poster &rarr; Publisher &rarr; Regular &rarr; <strong>Paid Creator</strong> &rarr; Sponsored &rarr; Showrunner &rarr; Headliner &rarr; <strong>Full-Time Creator</strong> &rarr; Institution.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>&#x1F69A; The local trade climbs&hellip;</h4>
        <p class="muted small">Odd Jobber &rarr; Kitted Out &rarr; Signwritten &rarr; Quoting &rarr; <strong>First Invoice</strong> &rarr; Regulars &rarr; Booked Out &rarr; Full Round &rarr; <strong>Own Boss</strong> &rarr; The One They Call.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>&#x1F3EA; The shop climbs&hellip;</h4>
        <p class="muted small">Daydreamer &rarr; Scouting &rarr; Pop-Up &rarr; Pitching the Concept &rarr; <strong>First Till Ring</strong> &rarr; Keyholder &rarr; Open Regular Hours &rarr; Rent Covered &rarr; <strong>Owner-Operator</strong> &rarr; Local Landmark.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>&#x2696;&#xFE0F; Same climb underneath</h4>
        <p class="muted small">Nine ladders, one game: identical XP on every rung, the same ten stages, and the same rule that nothing is bought with points. Rung 5 is always the first money. Rung 9 is always the day the job ends.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>&#x1F3AF; The gates fit the path</h4>
        <p class="muted small">A creator is never asked to register a company to take a sponsorship. A plumber is never asked for a pitch deck. Where a gate would be meaningless, that path gets an equivalent of exactly the same weight &mdash; never a free rung.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>&#x26A1; XP, streaks &amp; badges</h4>
        <p class="muted small">Every task, check-in, and quest earns XP. Rung-defining quests post to the public Wins wall &mdash; witnessed, not just claimed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="muted small" style="margin-top:1rem">In an accelerator program? The Ladder runs alongside it &mdash; levels 4 through 8 mirror the customer-discovery-to-pitch curriculum, and completing a program counts toward Level 9.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row">
  <div>
    <p class="hiw-step-label">Step 6</p>
    <h2>&#x1F310; Play multiplayer</h2>
    <p class="muted">Doing this alone, after work, is how it quietly stops. NoBossly is built to be played with witnesses &mdash; people at every rung, fitting it around the same kind of week you have, keeping score in public.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li><strong>Follow other members</strong> &mdash; see the quests and sprints they're working on, right in your feed</li>
      <li><strong>Cohort quests</strong> &mdash; one start date, one deadline, one leaderboard</li>
      <li><strong>The Wins wall</strong> &mdash; first dollars, first customers, resignation letters, witnessed</li>
      <li><strong>Forum</strong> &mdash; post questions, get feedback on your idea or copy between rungs</li>
      <li><strong>Member directory &amp; DMs</strong> &mdash; find members by level, connect directly</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="card" style="padding:1.5rem;align-self:center">
    <h4 style="margin:0 0 1rem">Your public profile</h4>
    <div class="profile-head" style="align-items:center;margin-bottom:1rem">
      <div class="avatar-circle">D</div>
      <div>
        <strong>Dillon Price</strong>
        <p class="muted small" style="margin:.2rem 0 0">&#x1F528; Level 3 &mdash; Builder &middot; &#x26A1; 325 XP</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin-bottom:.75rem">
      <span class="chip">&#x1F3C5; Shipped Something</span>
      <span class="chip">&#x1F3C5; Sprint 1 Complete</span>
      <span class="chip chip-success">&#x2705; Climbing to Operator</span>
    </div>
    <p class="muted small" style="margin:0">Bootstrapping a geo-flexible job board. &#x1F525; 12-day streak.</p>
  </div>
</section>

